  "reliabilityWarningTitle": "Before you start",
  "reliabilityWarningBody": "The flash takes several minutes and any USB drop or laptop sleep mid-flash leaves the MDB in an inconsistent state. Check:\n• A known-good USB cable, plugged in firmly at both ends. Flaky cables are the #1 cause of failed installs\n• Laptop on power, or fully charged. Battery saver / sleep can break the flash\n• Use a direct USB port, not a USB hub if possible\n• Don't unplug or move things around once the flash starts",
  "noPowerCycleWarningTitle": "DO NOT power-cycle anything during the install",
  "noPowerCycleWarningBody": "If something looks stuck, gives no feedback, or behaves oddly: stop and ask in Discord before doing anything else. Do not pull the AUX battery, disconnect the CBB, unplug USB, or restart the scooter or your laptop. The installer can recover from almost any state, as long as nothing interrupts it. Cutting power mid-flash is what bricks scooters.",
